    "created_at": "2022-12-16T16:46:21Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-12-16T16:46:21Z",
    "body": "My implementation in https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/pull/7730 is matching the `:user-*` pseudos between the last user-initiated form submission (if any) and the last user-initiated `change` event. If there isn't a user-initiated `change` event, the pseudos do not match.\r\n\r\nUser-initiated form submissions acts like a \"reset\" for the pseudo-class as the CSS spec defines: https://w3c.github.io/csswg-drafts/selectors/#user-pseudos\r\n\r\nFrom an user-POV this seems to match FF's behavior, though I haven't looked deeply into how it works. cc @emilio\r\n\r\nCan we spec it that way?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/1355201916/reactions",
